        "procedure": "Under nitrogen, PhSeSePh (630 mg, 2.01 mmol) and Hg (420 mg, 2.09 mmol) were stirred in pyridine (40 mL) for 24 h to give a clear yellow solution. Er (178 mg, 1.06 mmol) was added; after 14 h, NaN3 (65 mg, 1.00 mmol) and Na2O (73 mg, 1.17 mmol) were added. After 2 days the opaque greenish gray mixture was filtered to a yellow solution, concentrated (10 mL), and layered with hexanes (3 mL) in the dark to produce faint purple crystals (90 mg, 15%) that degrade at 85 °C, become a brown amorphous powder at 270 °C, and detonate at 336 °C.",
