        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Under nitrogen, Cd (110 mg, 2.09 mmol) and PhSeSePh (1300 mg, 4.16 mmol) were stirred in pyridine (50 mL) for 24 h to a dark yellow clear solution. Er (167 mg, 1.00 mmol) and Hg (50 mg, 0.25 mmol) were added; after 5 h the dark yellow-green solution was filtered to remove a gray precipitate. Elemental Se (160 mg, 2.02 mmol), NaN3 (65 mg, 1.05 mmol), and Na2O (63 mg, 1.01 mmol) were added; after 2 days the dark red solution was filtered to remove a yellow precipitate. Layering with hexanes in the dark gave pink-orange plates (60 mg, 4.2%) that flash and detonate at 312 °C. Crystallographic disorder arises from site sharing of SeSe and N3 ligands.",
